/-!
# Selective Case-II.1 residue data for p = 1831, q = 18311

This module is an independent auxiliary-prime receipt for comparison
with the existing q = 358877 receipt. The phase convention is exactly the
repository's real cycle generated by 3 modulo 1831.

The 915 entries use rho = 2^10 = 1024 modulo 18311,
W(x) = (1 - x)^10 / x^5, e_r = 915 * 3^r modulo 1831, and
phase[r] = log_rho (W(rho^e_r) / W(rho^915)).

Generated-vector SHA-256 (comma-separated decimal representatives):
07b37f3d2ec47e492dad3ba2ffe71ded2e05a099ec5250d6a4d7665bb8eb41e6.

The irregular numerical Fourier fact exposed here is actual frequency 278
(zero-based storage slot 277), whose coefficient is 1165 modulo 1831.  A
second regression records that regular frequency 636 vanishes. Thus this
auxiliary prime supports the selective channel proof but cannot support the
stronger full-determinant proof.
-/

namespace Fermat.OneThousandEightHundredThirtyOne.CircularUnitIrregularChannel1831AtQ18311

open Fermat.Irregular.CyclicDifferenceMatrix
